[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GNC-REQ-0001
TITLE: Bounded attitude experiment
STATUS: proposed
STATE: partial
STATEMENT: >>>
The GNC system shall execute a configured bounded multirotor attitude-estimation and control experiment without representing the experiment as full-flight capability.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Defines the single GNC product use while preventing extension scope from becoming an implicit obligation.
<<<
ACCEPTANCE: >>>
Inspection confirms the README scope statement includes the bounded experiment and excludes translation, flight, hardware and unactivated extensions.
<<<
EVIDENCE: README.md (scope); integration runner archived at tag pre-surgery-2026-11-22
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GNC-REQ-0030

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GNC-REQ-0002
TITLE: Deterministic configuration and replay
STATUS: proposed
STATE: partial
STATEMENT: >>>
The GNC system shall produce repeatable samples and state evolution for identical approved configuration, seed, initial state, input sequence, reset sequence and software revision.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Repeatability is required for engineering comparison and release evidence.
<<<
ACCEPTANCE: >>>
Two approved replays of the same component inputs produce identical outputs at the approved tolerance, and the configuration, seed and revision are recorded.
<<<
EVIDENCE: gnc_baseline/simulation/tests/test_components.py (component determinism); closed-loop replay archived at tag pre-surgery-2026-11-22
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GNC-REQ-0001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GNC-REQ-0003
TITLE: Runtime truth isolation
STATUS: proposed
STATE: partial
STATEMENT: >>>
The GNC system shall prevent live plant truth from entering estimator or controller runtime inputs after explicit initialization while permitting truth to reach sensor generation and independent evaluation.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Prevents circular validation and unrealistically privileged control or estimation.
<<<
ACCEPTANCE: >>>
Static interface inspection shows the estimator and controller public inputs contain no plant truth; a later integrated negative test is required.
<<<
EVIDENCE: gnc_baseline/estimation/estimator.py and gnc_baseline/control/controller.py (interfaces); integrated negative test not in active tree
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GNC-REQ-0001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GNC-REQ-0004
TITLE: Shared frames units and quaternion convention
STATUS: proposed
STATE: implemented
STATEMENT: >>>
The GNC system shall represent exchanged quantities using the NED and body frames, SI units, and scalar-first Hamilton quaternion convention.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A single convention prevents silent sign, frame and ordering defects across components.
<<<
ACCEPTANCE: >>>
Component analytical cases confirm every interface uses the scalar-first Hamilton convention.
<<<
EVIDENCE: gnc_baseline/simulation/quaternion.py; gnc_baseline/simulation/tests/test_components.py
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GNC-REQ-0001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GNC-REQ-0005
TITLE: Rigid-body rotational dynamics
STATUS: proposed
STATE: implemented
STATEMENT: >>>
The GNC plant shall propagate body angular velocity using the rigid-body rotational equation and a positive-definite inertia.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Defines the physical responsibility required by the bounded attitude experiment.
<<<
ACCEPTANCE: >>>
Zero-torque and principal-axis analytical cases match an independent equation oracle.
<<<
EVIDENCE: gnc_baseline/simulation/plant.py; gnc_baseline/simulation/tests/test_components.py
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GNC-REQ-0001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GNC-REQ-0006
TITLE: Quaternion plant state
STATUS: proposed
STATE: implemented
STATEMENT: >>>
The GNC plant shall propagate and normalize its scalar-first attitude quaternion using the body-rate and frame convention.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Attitude propagation must remain consistent with the shared representation.
<<<
ACCEPTANCE: >>>
Constant-rate analytical cases account for q/-q equivalence and confirm normalization.
<<<
EVIDENCE: gnc_baseline/simulation/plant.py; gnc_baseline/simulation/quaternion.py; gnc_baseline/simulation/tests/test_components.py
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GNC-REQ-0005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GNC-REQ-0007
TITLE: Paired torque command
STATUS: proposed
STATE: implemented
STATEMENT: >>>
The GNC controller shall publish one timestamped torque command that pairs requested torque, limited target and saturation status from the same controller due tick.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The pairing closes ambiguity between request, clamp result and anti-windup feedback.
<<<
ACCEPTANCE: >>>
Interface inspection and controller tests confirm the three fields and timestamp correspond to one due tick.
<<<
EVIDENCE: gnc_baseline/control/src/controller.cpp; gnc_baseline/control/controller.py; CTest gnc_controller_cpp_tests
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GNC-REQ-0016

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GNC-REQ-0008
TITLE: Limited-target actuator dynamics
STATUS: proposed
STATE: implemented
STATEMENT: >>>
The GNC actuator shall advance its response using only the held limited target from the latest eligible paired torque command.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Prevents a raw request from bypassing the controller's unique saturation responsibility.
<<<
ACCEPTANCE: >>>
Component tests compare the response with an independent first-order and clamp oracle.
<<<
EVIDENCE: gnc_baseline/simulation/actuator.py; gnc_baseline/simulation/tests/test_components.py
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GNC-REQ-0007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GNC-REQ-0009
TITLE: Actuator feedback pairing
STATUS: proposed
STATE: partial
STATEMENT: >>>
The GNC actuator shall publish actual torque and the originating paired-command timestamp in actuator feedback.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Controller anti-windup must associate actual response with the correct limited target.
<<<
ACCEPTANCE: >>>
A multi-rate interface test confirms feedback preserves the eligible command timestamp and corresponding limited target.
<<<
EVIDENCE: gnc_baseline/simulation/actuator.py (feedback fields not yet verified by a multi-rate test)
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GNC-REQ-0007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GNC-REQ-0010
TITLE: Gyroscope measurement
STATUS: proposed
STATE: implemented
STATEMENT: >>>
The GNC IMU shall produce timestamped body-frame angular-rate measurements with the approved bias, noise, validity and seed semantics.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Defines the estimator's angular-rate observation boundary.
<<<
ACCEPTANCE: >>>
Stationary, constant-rate, bias and deterministic-noise component cases match independent signal and random-sequence oracles.
<<<
EVIDENCE: gnc_baseline/simulation/imu.py; gnc_baseline/simulation/tests/test_components.py
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GNC-REQ-0001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GNC-REQ-0011
TITLE: Accelerometer specific force
STATUS: proposed
STATE: implemented
STATEMENT: >>>
The GNC IMU shall produce timestamped body-frame specific-force measurements using the gravity sign, bias, noise, validity and seed semantics.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Specific force rather than inertial acceleration is the estimator input.
<<<
ACCEPTANCE: >>>
Aligned and rotated stationary cases, bias and deterministic-noise cases match the independent specific-force equation and sign oracle.
<<<
EVIDENCE: gnc_baseline/simulation/imu.py; gnc_baseline/simulation/tests/test_components.py
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GNC-REQ-0001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GNC-REQ-0012
TITLE: Estimator propagation
STATUS: proposed
STATE: implemented
STATEMENT: >>>
The GNC estimator shall propagate and normalize a scalar-first attitude estimate from valid gyroscope samples and positive time increments.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Defines the attitude propagation responsibility of the estimator.
<<<
ACCEPTANCE: >>>
Component tests compare constant-rate propagation with an independent quaternion oracle and verify normalization and invalid-dt rejection.
<<<
EVIDENCE: gnc_baseline/estimation/estimator.py; gnc_baseline/estimation/tests/test_estimator.py
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GNC-REQ-0001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GNC-REQ-0013
TITLE: Roll and pitch fusion
STATUS: proposed
STATE: implemented
STATEMENT: >>>
The GNC estimator shall apply bounded accelerometer-based roll and pitch correction only when the validity and bounded-specific-force conditions permit it.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Gravity-based tilt correction is conditional and must not silently treat all acceleration as gravity.
<<<
ACCEPTANCE: >>>
Stationary-tilt and gated-contamination tests compare with an independent tilt oracle.
<<<
EVIDENCE: gnc_baseline/estimation/estimator.py; gnc_baseline/estimation/tests/test_estimator.py
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GNC-REQ-0012

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GNC-REQ-0014
TITLE: Yaw observability limitation
STATUS: proposed
STATE: implemented
STATEMENT: >>>
The GNC system shall report yaw as relative propagation and drift without claiming absolute yaw observability from gyroscope and accelerometer measurements alone.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Gravity provides no absolute heading reference.
<<<
ACCEPTANCE: >>>
Inspection confirms no absolute-yaw recovery claim is made by the estimator or its documentation.
<<<
EVIDENCE: gnc_baseline/estimation/estimator.py (no magnetometer or absolute heading input)
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GNC-REQ-0012

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GNC-REQ-0015
TITLE: Acceleration contamination handling
STATUS: proposed
STATE: partial
STATEMENT: >>>
The GNC estimator shall expose the correction-gating status when non-gravitational specific force violates its bounded tilt-correction assumptions.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The bounded attitude model lacks complete translational dynamics and must characterize rather than hide this limitation.
<<<
ACCEPTANCE: >>>
A contamination case observes the gating status and is classified as limitation characterization rather than performance pass.
<<<
EVIDENCE: gnc_baseline/estimation/estimator.py (gating); dedicated contamination case not in active tree
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GNC-REQ-0013

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GNC-REQ-0016
TITLE: Cascaded attitude and rate control
STATUS: proposed
STATE: implemented
STATEMENT: >>>
The GNC controller shall compute body-torque request through the attitude-error and body-rate feedback signs in a cascaded attitude and rate structure.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Defines the controller responsibility of the GNC experiment.
<<<
ACCEPTANCE: >>>
Unit tests use independent sign and axis oracles for positive and negative attitude and rate errors and reject the opposite-feedback mutation.
<<<
EVIDENCE: gnc_baseline/control/src/controller.cpp; gnc_baseline/control/tests/test_controller.cpp; CTest mutation tests
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GNC-REQ-0001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GNC-REQ-0017
TITLE: Unique controller saturation responsibility
STATUS: proposed
STATE: implemented
STATEMENT: >>>
The GNC controller shall be the sole component that limits requested body torque to the target bounds and sets the paired saturation status.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A single clamp authority prevents inconsistent targets and ambiguous feedback.
<<<
ACCEPTANCE: >>>
Boundary tests exercise every axis and confirm request, limited target and saturation status; no downstream component re-clamps the target.
<<<
EVIDENCE: gnc_baseline/control/src/controller.cpp; gnc_baseline/control/tests/test_controller.cpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GNC-REQ-0016

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GNC-REQ-0018
TITLE: Anti-windup update
STATUS: proposed
STATE: implemented
STATEMENT: >>>
The GNC controller shall update each rate-integral contribution using the conditional-integration and paired-feedback back-calculation rule and shall enforce the per-axis integral bounds.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The discrete rule must respond to both clamp saturation and actuator lag without silently accumulating beyond bounds.
<<<
ACCEPTANCE: >>>
Discrete-step tests independently calculate conditional integration, back-calculation and each axis bound.
<<<
EVIDENCE: gnc_baseline/control/src/controller.cpp; CTest mutation tests (antiwindup_disabled, antiwindup_backcalculation_sign_reversed)
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GNC-REQ-0016

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GNC-REQ-0019
TITLE: Invalid input rejection
STATUS: proposed
STATE: implemented
STATEMENT: >>>
The GNC system shall reject invalid, non-finite, stale, mis-shaped or non-positive-time inputs according to the owning component contract without silently advancing state.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Explicit rejection preserves state ownership and makes invalid trials auditable.
<<<
ACCEPTANCE: >>>
Negative-dt, stale-timestamp and representative invalid-value tests observe the rejection reason and unchanged owned state.
<<<
EVIDENCE: gnc_baseline/estimation/tests/test_estimator.py; gnc_baseline/control/python/tests/test_adapter.py
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GNC-REQ-0001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GNC-REQ-0020
TITLE: Reset contract
STATUS: proposed
STATE: partial
STATEMENT: >>>
The GNC system shall reset all stateful components to explicit initial state, seed and epoch-local scheduling while preserving the monotonically increasing scenario clock and discarding pre-reset held commands and feedback.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A single reset boundary is necessary for deterministic replay without stale state leakage.
<<<
ACCEPTANCE: >>>
A reset test verifies the reset tick, epoch-local first due updates, scenario timestamps and cleared held data.
<<<
EVIDENCE: gnc_baseline/control/python/tests/test_adapter.py (controller reset); integration-level reset tests archived at tag pre-surgery-2026-11-22
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GNC-REQ-0002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GNC-REQ-0021
TITLE: Deterministic scheduling and timestamps
STATUS: proposed
STATE: partial
STATEMENT: >>>
The GNC execution adapter shall schedule component updates and construct timestamps from integer base ticks using the due-phase, consumption and held-command rules.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The execution adapter owns ordering and prevents timing drift or ambiguous sample consumption.
<<<
ACCEPTANCE: >>>
A trace inspection and a multi-rate test match every produced and consumed sample to the sequence, period and timestamp rules.
<<<
EVIDENCE: execution runner and scheduler archived at tag pre-surgery-2026-11-22 (historical integration track)
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GNC-REQ-0002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GNC-REQ-0022
TITLE: Approved scenario suite
STATUS: proposed
STATE: planned
STATEMENT: >>>
The GNC system shall support the normal, initial-offset, signed-step, disturbance, noise-and-bias, saturation-withdrawal, acceleration-contamination, and invalid-input-and-reset scenarios.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
These scenarios bound the required engineering questions without extending to flight.
<<<
ACCEPTANCE: >>>
Each scenario has a purpose, required observations, applicable criteria and invalid-result handling defined in the scenario configuration.
<<<
EVIDENCE: no scenario execution in active tree; saturation-reachability negative finding recorded in tag pre-surgery-2026-11-22 (RESULTS.md)
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GNC-REQ-0001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GNC-REQ-0023
TITLE: Independent evaluation
STATUS: proposed
STATE: planned
STATEMENT: >>>
The GNC evaluator shall compute acceptance metrics independently of estimator and controller implementations using the approved raw signals, windows, units and invalid-data rules.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Independent oracles prevent the tested algorithm from grading itself.
<<<
ACCEPTANCE: >>>
Design inspection identifies a distinct oracle for each verification provision.
<<<
EVIDENCE: no evaluator in active tree
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GNC-REQ-0001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GNC-REQ-0024
TITLE: Evidence provenance
STATUS: proposed
STATE: planned
STATEMENT: >>>
Any reported result shall identify software revision, configuration hash, scenario, seed, environment, command, raw artifact location and terminal result.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A pass or fail statement without provenance is not reproducible evidence.
<<<
ACCEPTANCE: >>>
Each retained result record contains every listed provenance field; records missing a field are rejected by inspection.
<<<
EVIDENCE: no result records in active tree
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GNC-REQ-0001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GNC-REQ-0025
TITLE: Defect-detection demonstration
STATUS: proposed
STATE: partial
STATEMENT: >>>
The GNC release shall demonstrate that selected independent checks detect isolated sign, unit, quaternion-ordering or anti-windup defects without modifying the production baseline.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A limited mutation demonstration provides evidence that critical checks are capable of failing.
<<<
ACCEPTANCE: >>>
Isolated variants are compiled and the expected checks fail; the production baseline is unchanged.
<<<
EVIDENCE: gnc_baseline/control/tests/test_controller.cpp and four mutation executables (CTest); quaternion-ordering and unit mutations not yet added
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GNC-REQ-0024

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GNC-REQ-0026
TITLE: Implementation language boundary
STATUS: proposed
STATE: implemented
STATEMENT: >>>
The GNC control core shall be implemented in C++17, and Python shall be limited to simulation, orchestration and analysis through a declared interface boundary.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Preserves a portable control core while retaining productive analysis tooling.
<<<
ACCEPTANCE: >>>
The CMake build compiles the control core as C++17 and the Python binding exposes only the declared functions.
<<<
EVIDENCE: gnc_baseline/control/CMakeLists.txt; gnc_baseline/control/python/controller_bindings.cpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GNC-REQ-0001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GNC-REQ-0027
TITLE: Clean-checkout reproduction
STATUS: proposed
STATE: planned
STATEMENT: >>>
The GNC release shall be reproducible from a clean checkout using documented dependency versions and commands without relying on untracked developer state.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A local green workspace is insufficient release evidence.
<<<
ACCEPTANCE: >>>
A clean clone installs pinned dependencies, runs the documented commands and reproduces the test results.
<<<
EVIDENCE: pinned dependencies in requirements.txt and CMakePresets.json; clean-clone run not yet executed
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GNC-REQ-0024

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GNC-REQ-0028
TITLE: Legacy control disposition
STATUS: proposed
STATE: implemented
STATEMENT: >>>
The GNC system shall record CTL-REQ-001 and CTL-REQ-002 as historical references, not as GNC criteria, and shall attach no satisfaction claim to them.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Preserves historical identifiers while preventing incompatible legacy thresholds from silently becoming GNC criteria. The original legacy requirement file was removed from the active tree by the lean-restructuring PR and remains in git history at tag pre-surgery-2026-11-22.
<<<
ACCEPTANCE: >>>
Inspection confirms both identifiers are listed here as historical, carry no pass state and that no GNC requirement reuses their thresholds.
<<<
EVIDENCE: this file (requirements/gnc.sdoc)
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GNC-REQ-0001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GNC-REQ-0029
TITLE: Invalid measurement handling
STATUS: proposed
STATE: partial
STATEMENT: >>>
The GNC estimator and controller shall not consume an invalid or stale measurement as a valid update and shall expose the rejection or hold status.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Validity must affect consumption rather than serving as passive metadata.
<<<
ACCEPTANCE: >>>
Component tests inject invalid and stale samples and confirm no valid update occurs and the status is observable.
<<<
EVIDENCE: gnc_baseline/estimation/tests/test_estimator.py; integration-level injection archived at tag pre-surgery-2026-11-22
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GNC-REQ-0019

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GNC-REQ-0030
TITLE: GNC exclusion boundary
STATUS: proposed
STATE: implemented
STATEMENT: >>>
The GNC system shall exclude position and velocity loops, waypoint flight, full INS or GNSS estimation, advanced-control comparisons, learning algorithms, embedded targets, HIL and flight claims unless a separately approved extension activates them.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Makes the stopping rule reviewable and prevents extensions from expanding GNC implicitly.
<<<
ACCEPTANCE: >>>
Inspection of the active tree finds no activated excluded capability and no unsupported flight, HIL, hardware or research claim.
<<<
EVIDENCE: README.md (scope and exclusions)
